        <span itemprop="definition">high-density polyethylene</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0071">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">a polyethylene composition</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">composed of 20 weight % of an ultra-high-molecular-weight polyethylene (UHMWPE) having a weight-average molecular weight of 2.0 ⁇ 10 6 and 80 weight % of a high-density polyethylene (HDPE) having a weight-average molecular weight of 3.3 ⁇ 10 5 was incorporated with 0.375 weight parts of an antioxidant based on 100 weight parts of the polyethylene composition, to prepare a polyethylene composition (melting point: 135° C., crystal dispersion temperature: 90° C.)</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0072">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">a mixture composed of 30 weight parts of the polyethylene composition and 5 weight parts of polyethylene wax</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">Mitsubishi Chemicals</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0072">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the resulting solution</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was extruded from the T-die attached at the extruder end in such a way to have 25  ⁇ m as thickness of the final product, and taken up by a cooling roll, kept at 50° C., to prepare a gel-like sheet.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0072">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the sheet</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was then biaxially stretched at 115° C. at an areal stretching ratio of 5 by 5, to prepare the stretched sheet.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0072">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the sheet</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was thermally set at 122° C. for 10 seconds, to prepare a polyethylene membrane.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0072">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the resulting membrane</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">was washed with methylene chloride to remove the residual liquid paraffin by extraction and dried to prepare a 25  ⁇ m thick microporous polyethylene membrane.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0072">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">Table 2</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">The properties of the membrane are shown in Table 2.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0072">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">a polyethylene composition</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">(melting point: 165° C., crystal dispersion temperature: 90° C.), composed of 20 weight % of an ultra-high-molecular-weight polyethylene (UHMWPE) having a weight-average molecular weight of 2.5 ⁇ 10 6 , 60 weight % of a high-density polyethylene (HDPE) having a weight-average molecular weight of 3.5 ⁇ 10 5 and 20 weight % of a polyethylene having a weight-average molecular weight of 5.1 ⁇ 10 5 was incorporated with 0.375 weight parts of an antioxidant based on 100 weight parts of the polyethylene composition, to prepare a polyethylene composition.</span>
